Two cyclists travel away from a checkpoint along straight paths. Describe how each cyclist’s distance from the checkpoint and speed change. Explain using the steepness of each curve.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{scope}
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(3.4,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,3.3);
\draw[graphblue,thick] (0,0) .. controls (1,0) and (2.2,1.2) .. (3,3);
\node[above] at (1.6,3.3) {A};
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.55,1.65) {Distance from checkpoint};
\node[below] at (1.7,-0.15) {Time};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[xshift=52mm]
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(3.4,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,3.3);
\draw[graphblue,thick] (0,0) .. controls (0.7,2.1) and (2,2.8) .. (3,2.9);
\node[above] at (1.6,3.3) {B};
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.55,1.65) {Distance from checkpoint};
\node[below] at (1.7,-0.15) {Time};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two walkers return towards a shelter along straight paths. Describe how each walker’s distance from the shelter and speed change. Explain using the steepness of each curve.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{scope}
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(3.4,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,3.3);
\draw[graphblue,thick] (0,3) .. controls (1,3) and (2.2,1.8) .. (3,0);
\node[above] at (1.6,3.3) {A};
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.55,1.65) {Distance from shelter};
\node[below] at (1.7,-0.15) {Time};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[xshift=52mm]
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(3.4,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,3.3);
\draw[graphblue,thick] (0,3) .. controls (0.7,0.9) and (2,0.3) .. (3,0.2);
\node[above] at (1.6,3.3) {B};
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.55,1.65) {Distance from shelter};
\node[below] at (1.7,-0.15) {Time};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The graph shows Leila’s distance from a cabin as she travels along a straight path. For each labelled stage, describe:
(a) whether her distance from the cabin increases, decreases or stays the same;
(b) whether the gradient is positive, negative or zero, and constant or varying;
(c) her direction and how her speed changes.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(14.7,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,4.1);
\draw[graphblue,thick] (0,0) .. controls (0.67,0) and (1.33,0.33) .. (2,1);
\draw[graphblue,thick] (2,1)--(4,3);
\draw[graphblue,thick] (4,3) .. controls (4.67,3.67) and (5.33,4) .. (6,4);
\draw[graphblue,thick] (6,4)--(8,4);
\draw[graphblue,thick] (8,4) .. controls (8.67,4) and (9.33,3.67) .. (10,3);
\draw[graphblue,thick] (10,3)--(12,1);
\draw[graphblue,thick] (12,1) .. controls (12.67,0.33) and (13.33,0) .. (14,0);
\node at (1,0.7) {A};
\node at (3,2.45) {B};
\node at (5,3.25) {C};
\node at (7,3.65) {D};
\node at (9,3.25) {E};
\node at (11,2.45) {F};
\node at (13,0.7) {G};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.2,2) {Distance from cabin};
\node[below] at (7.2,-0.15) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
